        <mxCell id="p0-onemodel-13" value="&lt;b&gt;Why OMNeT++ without INET (ADR)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;the experiments need queues, links, delays and partitions — not a full TCP/IP stack&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;a shared C++ core keeps the simulated logic identical to the Go logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;iFogSim / Fogify model resource placement well, but not credentials, caches and trust&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=0;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="p0-1">
